{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For TS recruitment, the first step is to advise unsuccessful candidates."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the process initiation and the first explicit action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are \"no more candidates\", then the position should be re-advertised."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the candidate availability check; correctly routes 'No' (meaning no more candidates) to re-advertising."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "guard:b2->n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the terms and conditions of the offer for a candidate need to be sorted out, it is necessary to check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the voluntary redundancy check and the resulting decision split."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the candidate has accepted, further investigation is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly models the positive outcome branch requiring further investigation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The recruitment manager sends an Appointment Approval form, which is then received by the next level manager."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of sending the approval form upon a negative redundancy check."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7",
        "guard:b3->n8",
        "guard:b3->n9",
        "action:n8",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form. However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Splits based on external vs. existing status; 'No' (existing) continues, 'Yes' (external) handles the authorization/approval path. Behaviour preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The HR department scans the completed form and records the position against the stored position in GovSource."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the scanning and recording step after form approval."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15",
        "guard:b5->n16",
        "guard:b5->n17",
        "action:n16",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are any variations, a complete business case is required. Otherwise, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Checks for variations; routes 'Yes' to creating a business case, 'No' to continuing the process."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the position requires a medical assessment, it is applicable for a 12% rate. Otherwise, a medical assessment is not necessary.",
        "For the step of the Preferred Candidate's medical assessments, it is important to note that it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly checks for the 12% rate requirement and incorporates the 21-day timeframe into the affirmative branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the position requires a medical assessment, it is applicable for a 12% rate. Otherwise, a medical assessment is not necessary.",
        "For the step of the Preferred Candidate's medical assessments, it is important to note that it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly checks for the 12% rate requirement and incorporates the 21-day timeframe into the affirmative branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->c2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the position requires a medical assessment, it is applicable for a 12% rate. Otherwise, a medical assessment is not necessary.",
        "For the step of the Preferred Candidate's medical assessments, it is important to note that it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly checks for the 12% rate requirement and incorporates the 21-day timeframe into the affirmative branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the position requires a medical assessment, it is applicable for a 12% rate. Otherwise, a medical assessment is not necessary.",
        "For the step of the Preferred Candidate's medical assessments, it is important to note that it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly checks for the 12% rate requirement and incorporates the 21-day timeframe into the affirmative branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The TS HR coordinator informs the recruitment manager, who then liaises with the HR representative to confirm the offer to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the coordination and liaison steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n21",
        "guard:b7->n22",
        "guard:b7->n23",
        "action:n22",
        "action:n23"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the assessment is not satisfactory, the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted. However, if the assessment is fine, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Evaluates assessment satisfaction; 'No' triggers contacting the next candidate, 'Yes' continues the flow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n24"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The recruitment manager makes a formal verbal offer of employment to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for making the verbal offer."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n25",
        "guard:b8->n26",
        "guard:b8->n27",
        "action:n26",
        "action:n27"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the candidate accepts, the recruitment manager creates a formal written offer. If the candidate declines, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Splits on candidate acceptance; 'Yes' produces the written offer, 'No' proceeds forward."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n28"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, the commencement pack and letter of appointment are sent to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Uses an AND gateway to model the simultaneous dispatch of documents, preserving concurrent behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n29",
        "guard:b9->n30",
        "guard:b9->c4",
        "action:n30"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the candidate receives these documents, if there is a \"40%\" rate, renegotiation is required. Otherwise, if the candidate accepts, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Checks for the 40% rate condition; 'Yes' initiates renegotiation, 'No' continues the process."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n31",
        "guard:b10->n32",
        "guard:b10->n33",
        "action:n32",
        "action:n33"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the renegotiation is successful, the process continues. However, if the renegotiation is unsuccessful, the next candidate on the shortlist should be identified."
      ],
      "justification": "Evaluates renegotiation outcome; 'Yes' continues, 'No' triggers identification of the next candidate."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly marks the termination of the process flow."
    }
  ],
